title: upload/download and read-mode open hold whole files in memory
updated: 2026-08-13T05:02:10Z
---

Fs::LibSSH::upload slurps the local file, download slurps the remote one, and File::LibSSH::open in < mode buffers the entire remote file locally before read()/seek() operate on it.

Fine for config files, not for anything large. Either document the limit in POD or chunk through Channel::read($len)/write. Note Net::LibSSH::Channel::read(undef) reads nothing -- undef numifies to 0; pass -1 or no argument.
